[36m(main_task pid=4109237)[0m  Wenger returned to England in 2000 to take charge of Arsenal, the club where he had played for six seasons in the 1980s, succeeding George Graham. In his first seven seasons, Arsenal won the Premier League title in 2002, 2003 and 2005, the FA Cup in 2002 and 2005, the League Cup in 2001 and 2003 and the Inter-Troféu Da Taça da Liga Portuguesa in 2002 (a trophy awarded to the Premier League champions upon their first visit to Portugal). In 2005–06 Arsenal finished top of the Premier League table, but lost in the 2006 FA Cup Final, and 2006 League Cup Final. Wenger's teams have also featured some of the fastest attacks and highest goal-scoring averages in top-flight history. Despite never finishing outside the top four in the Premier League, Wenger has been widely criticised for his failure to win the Champions League, often considered the "Holy Grail" of club football, as Arsenal came close on a number of occasions, losing in the final in 2000, 2006, 2007 and 2014.</information>
